From 13241529bc7faa7920b2ce9e77ca25d049bd787f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Harshit Gupta <39994376+arelyx@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 08:30:14 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno/a2xx: per-pixel loop exit for divergent breaks on
 Xenos

A predicated control-flow instruction decides for all 64 pixels of a
sequencer: (p0) is taken if any pixel has p0, (!p0) only if none has
(Xenia's ucode.h, from the sequencer specification). A break inside an if
was a (p0) jump, so one pixel breaking took every pixel out of the loop.

For innermost loops without discard whose breaks can diverge (NIR
divergence analysis), a register holds 1.0 while the pixel is in the
loop: the body is predicated on it, a break clears it under the current
predicate, code after a breaking if is predicated again, and the back
edge, under that predicate, is a (p0) jump taken while any pixel is
still active. Predicated-off pixels keep their registers.

dEQP shaders.return.return_in_dynamic_loop_dynamic_{vertex,fragment}
pass. Nested loops and loops with discard keep plain jumps (both hung:
a killed pixel keeps active set). Uniform loops keep plain jumps (17%
slower in glmark2's uniform loop otherwise).

